# {{ project_name | replace('_', ' ') | title }}

A Streamlit app running on [Databricks Apps](https://docs.databricks.com/en/dev-tools/databricks-apps/index.html), scaffolded by [dex](https://github.com/yarrib/dex).

Databricks Apps are hosted web applications that run within your Databricks workspace. They have native access to Unity Catalog, SQL warehouses, and the Databricks SDK — no extra authentication needed.

## Setup

```bash
uv sync
```

## Project Structure

```
{{ project_name }}/
├── app/
│   ├── app.py              # Streamlit entry point
│   ├── auth.py             # Databricks OAuth helper
│   └── requirements.txt    # App runtime dependencies (used by Databricks Apps)
├── tests/                  # Tests
├── databricks.yml          # Databricks Asset Bundle config
└── pyproject.toml          # Local dev dependencies
```

## Local Development

Run the app locally (requires Databricks CLI auth configured):

```bash
streamlit run app/app.py
```

Run tests:

```bash
uv run pytest
```

Lint and format:

```bash
uv run ruff check .
uv run ruff format .
```

## Deploy

```bash
# Deploy to dev (default target)
databricks bundle deploy

# Deploy to staging
databricks bundle deploy --target staging

# Deploy to prod
databricks bundle deploy --target prod

# Run (open the app URL)
databricks bundle run {{ project_name }}_app
```

## Configuration

The bundle uses the following variables (set via `--var` or `databricks.yml` overrides):

| Variable | Description | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `workspace_url` | Databricks workspace URL | _(required)_ |
| `catalog` | Unity Catalog catalog name | `dev` / `staging` / `prod` |
| `schema` | Unity Catalog schema name | `{{ project_name }}_dev` |
{% if not warehouse_id %}| `warehouse_id` | SQL warehouse ID for data queries | _(required)_ |
{% endif %}

Set workspace URL before deploying:

```bash
databricks bundle deploy --var workspace_url=https://<your-workspace>.azuredatabricks.net
```
